    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d538">

                <pb facs="0565" n="457" xml:id="pg457"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.841 Surtax/46: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in China</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">MacMurray</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-12-17T16:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">December 17,
                                1927—4 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>416. Shanghai despatch to the Department No. 4948, September 9, 1927, page
                        16.<anchor n="11" xml:id="d538-f1"/></p>
                <p>What disposition has been made of tonnage dues deposited with the American
                    Consulate General at Shanghai?</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d538-f1" n="11" xml:id="d538-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; the pertinent portion of the despatch reads: “I am still holding the
                    certified cheque covering the treaty tonnage dues on the S. S. <hi
                        rendition="#italic">President McKinley</hi>, as well as the dues deposited
                    on the other four vessels. The Consular Body will meet on September 13 to
                    discuss a proposal to utilize the treaty tonnage dues deposited with the
                    Consulates to offset the tonnage surtax payments made under protest by the
                    depositors. I am not in sympathy with this proposal but out of courtesy to my
                    colleagues and at their request I have consented to hold the dues deposited with
                    me until this proposal has been discussed.” (File No. 893.841 Surtax/45.)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
